From: AX6 local correctness review <local@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ssdk: avoid MIB I/O when no physical port exists

The sampler starts at physical port 1. A topology with ports <= 1 has
no physical port in its exclusive range, so normalizing the cursor to
port 1 must not cause a read outside that range. Leave state and hardware
untouched in this case. Do not change normal polling or work ownership.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/ref/ref_mib.c
+++ b/src/ref/ref_mib.c
@@ -511,6 +511,9 @@ qca_ar8327_sw_mib_task(struct qca_phy_priv *priv)
 {
 	int ret;
 
+	if (priv->ports <= SSDK_PHYSICAL_PORT1)
+		return;
+
 	mutex_lock(&priv->reg_mutex);
 	/* Port 0 is the CPU/non-physical port; it has no MIB and returns
 	 * SW_OUT_OF_RANGE. Start at the first physical port.
